  "id": "Compound::DB00908 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Quinidine and Cyp2c8, mediated through the antimalarial alkaloid Cinchona Alkaloid. Quinidine is linked to several conditions, including blindness, angina, and blackwater fever, all of which are associated with Quinine. Quinine binds to Cyp2c8, and this binding is observed across multiple paths, indicating a possible functional interaction. The shared lowest common ancestor, Cinchona Alkaloid, underscores the common pathway involving antimalarial agents. The scores from the paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological mechanism. However, the evidence is limited to the observed interactions and does not provide direct evidence of a direct interaction between Quinidine and Cyp2c8. The mechanism appears to involve Quinine as a mediator, but further studies are needed to confirm the exact role of Quinidine in this relationship.",
